+### 2.4 Bounded protected-path delivery amendment (adopted as fallback)
+
+To remove the Act 6 §2 objection rather than argue it, this Act amends
+`government/reviewed-merge.sh` with **one named allowlist** for this Act's own
+enactment delivery only. The amendment is operative **only** when all of the
+following hold:
+
+1. the change is the enactment implementation of Act 25 and nothing else;
+2. `records/suite-status.json` records `run-all` **and** `ballot-integrity`
+   green on the exact candidate commit/tree being merged;
+3. a non-sponsor, non-Clerk reviewer records that the diff is confined to the
+   allowlist below;
+4. no ballot row, seat, vote value, quorum or outcome is changed.
+
+Allowlist (exactly these paths, nothing else):
+`records/bills/executive-innovation-office-act.md` (the restoration),
+`records/ENACTMENT-STATUS.md`, `records/bills/executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v2.md`,
+the dated erratum/addendum records for this Act, and `government/LAWS.md`.
+
+Any other protected path is still refused exactly as today. Only the Clerk (or a
+delegate recorded under Act 6.2) may invoke the allowlisted path, and only after
+conditions 2 and 3 are recorded. The amendment itself is a `government/` change:
+it is included in the Phase 1 combined change and lands by the §2.3/§4 verified
+fast-forward, so it is in force for Phase 2's `LAWS.md` codification, which then
+goes through the **ordinary reviewed-merge path** rather than a bypass.
+
